  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(x2 - (1)/(x²)) = 4√6 = (x + (1)/(x))(x - (1)/(x)) ...(1)\n\nsquaring both sides\n\n⇒ (x² - (1)/(x²))² = 16 × 6\n\n⇒ x4 + (1)/(x⁴) - 2 = 96\n\n⇒ x4 + (1)/(x⁴) = 98\n\n⇒ x4 + (1)/(x⁴) + 2 = 98 + 2\n\n⇒ (x2 + (1)/(x²))² = 100\n\n⇒ x2 + (1)/(x²) = 10\n\n⇒ x2 + (1)/(x²) + 2 = 10 + 2\n\n⇒ (x + (1)/(x))² = 12\n\n⇒ x + (1)/(x) = √12 = 2√3 ...(2)\n\nso\n\n⇒ x - (1)/(x) = 2√2 [after dividing equation (1) by (2)]\n\nand\n\n(x - (1)/(x))3 = (x3 - (1)/(x³)) - 3 (x - (1)/(x))\n\n⇒ (2√2)³ = x3 - (1)/(x³) - 3(2√2)\n\n⇒ 16√2 + 6√2 = x3 - (1)/(x³) \n\n⇒ x3 - (1)/(x³) = 22√2",
